# Import / Bake: Change Only What You Need

When bringing Blockbench/glTF props into `samples/open-world-rpg` or fixing one asset’s faces/scale/atlas:

## Rules

1. **Name the targets.** Bake with an explicit filter: `python tools/bake_tier1_props_gltf.py outrider_shortbow` — never run the baker with no args unless the owner asked to rebake everything.
2. **Do not rewrite unrelated runtime files.** Leave other `assets/models/*.gltf` / `*.png`, prefabs, and world placements alone unless the task names them.
3. **Baker defaults stay conservative.** New winding/atlas/double-side behavior must be **opt-in per `PROPS` entry** (`double_sided`, `double_sided_thin`, `clean_backdrop`, `max_atlas`, …). Do not change global bake heuristics in a way that alters bush/crate/campfire/etc. when those props are rebaked later.
4. **Before/after scope check.** After a bake or copy, `git status` on `assets/models/` (and prefabs) and revert anything outside the requested set.
5. **Texture atlases are sacred.** Do not “fix” another prop’s PNG/atlas while importing a weapon. Prefer `clean_backdrop: False` / higher `max_atlas` only on the prop that needs it.
6. **Recover collateral damage.** If a prior step touched extras (e.g. `bush.png`), restore from git immediately: `git checkout HEAD -- path/to/file`.

## Examples

```text
❌ BAD: python tools/bake_tier1_props_gltf.py
        (rebakes every PROPS entry; risks atlas/winding drift on shipping props)

✅ GOOD: python tools/bake_tier1_props_gltf.py outrider_shortbow ashfell_arming_sword

❌ BAD: Change bake_tier1_props_gltf.py so ALL prims auto double-side / new UV snap
✅ GOOD: Add "double_sided_thin": True only on outrider_shortbow’s PROPS entry

❌ BAD: Notice bush.png dirty after a sword import and leave it
✅ GOOD: git checkout HEAD -- samples/open-world-rpg/assets/models/bush.png bush.gltf
```

